error[E0401]: `x` is `own`, so it must be used exactly once, but `twice_owned` may use it more than once
  --> own_param.ck:14:16
   |
14 | fn twice_owned x -> p : x~own a, p~(a, a)
   |                ^
   = help: `own` promises a single use, so the argument may be a resource; remove `own` if the value must be used twice

error[E0401]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), so it must be used exactly once, but `generic_without_own` may use it more than once
  --> own_param.ck:17:24
   |
17 | fn generic_without_own f : f~File
   |                        ^
   = note: `f` is passed to `keep`, whose parameter is not `own`, so `keep` may copy or drop it
   = help: mark that parameter of `keep` with `own` (as in `x~own a`) so it can take a resource

warning[W010]: `own` is implied: `File` holds a resource
  --> own_param.ck:23:22
   |
23 | fn implied f : f~own File
   |                      ^^^^ this `own` can go
   = help: remove `own`; a resource is used exactly once anyway

error[E0357]: `own` on `Nat`, which holds no resource
  --> own_param.ck:26:29
   |
26 | fn pointless n -> m : n~own Nat, m~Nat
   |                             ^^^ `own` has no use here
   = help: `own` is for generic parameters that may receive a resource, as in `v~own a`; remove it

own_param.ck: 3 errors, 1 warning
